.TH ANSIBLE\-TEMPLE 1 "October 2026" "ansible-temple 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ansible\-temple \- choose a service from a playbook catalogue and deploy it locally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ansible\-temple
.RI [ repository ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ansible\-temple
reads a Git repository that publishes an Ansible catalogue.
The repository has
.I manifest.json
at its root and one directory per service under
.IR playbooks/ ,
each with
.I info.json
and
.IR main.yml .
.PP
The program lists the services on the full width of the terminal.
Opening a service shows the options declared in the catalogue, the
repository address, and the playbook path.
.B Deploy
runs
.BR ansible\-playbook (1)
on this machine.
.PP
The reference catalogue is
.UR https://github.com/elestranobaron/wp\-package\-installator\-playbooks
.UE .
Another repository is accepted when it follows the same layout.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I repository
Clone or update this catalogue instead of asking for an address.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ansible\-temple/repository
Last catalogue address.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ansible\-temple/catalog
Checkout of the catalogue.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up / Down
Move.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected service, edit a field, or deploy.
.TP
.B Escape / q
Go back, or quit from the list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the program stops without a failed deploy; the exit status of
.B ansible\-playbook
when a deploy was started; 2 on usage or catalogue errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ansible\-playbook (1),
.BR git (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Thomas Lloancy
